{key: Bb}
{tempo: 71}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |
| [F7sus4] | [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |
| [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Praise the [Bb]LORD, O my [Gm7]soul
I will [Eb]praise Him as [F]long as I [Bb]live
I will sing praise to my [Gm7]God
As [Eb]long as I have [F]breath in my [Bb]lungs
Do [Gm]not put your [F]trust in prin[Eb]ces
In [Gm]mortals who [F]cannot [Eb]save
When their [Gm]breath de[F]parts from [Eb]them
They [Cm7]return to the dust be[F]low
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Praise the [Bb]LORD, O my [Gm7]soul
I will [Eb]praise Him as [F]long as I [Bb]live
I will sing praise to [F/A]my [Gm7]God
As [Eb]long as I [F]have breath in my [Bb]lungs
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |
| [Fsus4] [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]On that [Bb]day all their [Gm7]plans
Come to [Eb]nothing [F]in the [Bb]end [F/A]
[Gm7]Blessed is the one whose [F]help
[Eb]Is the God of Jacob's name
[Cm7]Whose hope is in the LORD
His [F]God, the living One
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Praise the LORD, O [F/A]my [Gm7]soul
As [Eb]long as I have [F]breath [Bb]
